:"CTB-50L17.10","gene_symbol_current":"HDGFL2","gene_id":"ENSG00000167674","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"unclear","nucleus_padj":0.370037,"nucleus_log2fc":0.0185726,"nucleus_score":-1.04435,"pct_ad":0.188846,"pct_control":0.197081,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.986262,"donor_log2fc":0.0510131,"donor_lfcse":0.114868,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":3.96062e-06},{"cell_type":"In","gene_symbol":"CTB-50L17.10","gene_symbol_current":"HDGFL2","gene_id":"ENSG00000167674","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999889,"donor_log2fc":0.121656,"donor_lfcse":0.195065,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":3.21534e-06}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000167674","entrez_id":["84717"],"uniprot":["Q7Z4V5"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a member of the hepatoma-derived growth factor (HDGF) family. The protein includes an N-terminal PWWP domain that binds to methyl-lysine-containing histones, with specific binding of this protein to tri-methylated lysines 36 and 79 of histone H3, and di- and tri-methylated lysine 20 of histone H4. The protein functions in LEDGF/p75-independent HIV-1 replication by determining HIV-1 integration site selection. Alternative splicing of this gene results in multiple transcript variants. [provided by RefSeq, Apr 2014].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q7Z4V5","text":"Acts as an epigenetic regulator of myogenesis in cooperation with DPF3a (isoform 2 of DPF3/BAF45C) (PubMed:32459350). Associates with the BAF complex via its interaction with DPF3a and HDGFL2-DPF3a activate myogenic genes by increasing chromatin accessibility through recruitment of SMARCA4/BRG1/BAF190A (ATPase subunit of the BAF complex) to myogenic gene promoters (PubMed:32459350). Promotes the repair of DNA double-strand breaks (DSBs) through the homologous recombination pathway by facilitating the recruitment of the DNA endonuclease RBBP8 to the DSBs (PubMed:26721387). Preferentially binds to chromatin regions marked by H3K9me3, H3K27me3 and H3K36me2 (PubMed:26721387, PubMed:32459350). Involved in cellular growth control, through the regulation of cyclin D1 expression (PubMed:25689719)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}